\section{The Basics}\label{section-6-basics}
Matrix multiplication is a fundamental operation in linear algebra. It is
defined as the dot product of two vectors, but for matrices. The
result is a matrix, and the operation is associative, meaning that the
order in which you multiply matrices does not matter.

